      "spam": false,
      "value": "Time synced events, and time queued events, are something many online games have. For example a Soccer mini-game in an old MMO called Phantasy Star Online uses time events to coordinate the syncronization aspect and the start and end aspect of the minigame.\n\nThings such as time scheduled events could allow for the implementation of day-night cycles which could take advantage of the realtime precomputed Enlighten GI. There are a lot of neat things that can be done to increase the livelyness aspect of a world if given the ability to queue or schedule time events.\n\nI would suggest implementing a server time and then synchronizing it between clients. The PSO client syncronizes it on login and then uses a snapshot at that time and diffs it to produce the current time. A simple yet powerful system that can provide value to many world creators!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
